<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This approach has served me well=
 when building interfaces that need to be both <strong>highly interactive a=
nd maintainable at scale</strong>.</p>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Part 2: Deep Tec=
hnical Discussion</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: I'=
m impressed by your compositional approach. Let's dive deeper into state ma=
nagement since that's crucial for our authorization platform. At Webflow, w=
e're dealing with complex permission trees, real-time collaboration, and vi=
sual editor state. How would you approach state architecture for a system w=
here permissions can affect what users can edit, what they can see, and how=
 they collaborate?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is a fascinating challenge because you're dealing with <strong>multiple st=
ate domains that have complex interdependencies</strong>. Let me break down=
 how I'd approach this:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>State Domain Analysis:</=
strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Authorization State</st=
rong> - User permissions, role hierarchies, resource access</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Editor State</strong> -=
 Canvas elements, selection, tools, history</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Collaboration State</st=
rong> - Other users, cursor positions, real-time changes</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>UI State</strong> - Pan=
el visibility, modals, loading states</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Architecture Strategy: D=
omain-Driven State Management</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I'd recommend a <strong>hybrid a=
pproach</strong> that leverages different state management tools for their =
strengths:</p>
