 Use React DevTools Profiler, Chrome DevTools, and Core Web Vitals</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Progressive Loading</st=
rong>: Load what's needed when it's needed</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Efficient Updates</stro=
ng>: Minimize re-renders through proper state design</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Hardware Acceleration</=
strong>: Use GPU for animations and effects</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory Awareness</stron=
g>: Clean up unused resources proactively</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This approach has allowed me to =
maintain <strong>60fps interactions</strong> even with complex projects con=
taining thousands of elements, which is essential for the creative workflow=
 that Webflow enables.</p>
